  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1924; the four retiring members were returned unopposed (Northern Whig, 7 January 1924, p. 8). 'COOKSTOWN—NO CONTEST. Messrs. George Ferguson, Jun.; David H. Hamilton, Samuel M'Kinney, and John Scott.' All four were retiring members nominated by the Unionist Association and were the only candidates. Returned unopposed."
